<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm4b-jiuquan ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 4B / Yaogan 53-07..09 + 56-19..21 (Jiuquan) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
No public LM-4B altitude/velocity table found (LM-4B event TIMES only: S1 shutdown 153.06s, S3 shutdown 648.68s, SC sep 718.68s for Y51/LEO, huijiwiki).
Closest family member with a published loft: LM-3B (same CALT hypergolic YF-21 core heritage). Loft: SURROGATE — LM-3B typical GTO trajectory, CALT &#x27;LM-3A Series Launch Vehicles User&#x27;s Manual&#x27; Issue 2011, Tables 3-5/3-6
(event time s, flight altitude km, ground range km), liftoff altitude 1.8 km removed. Cut at Stage-3 first shutdown T+615.7 s, 204.3 km, 2466.2 km.
Source: http://www.georing.biz/usefull/LM-3A%20Series%20Launch%20Vehicles%20User&#x27;s%20Manual%20Issue%202011.pdf
Ground range IS published, so no Rel.Vel split is needed; velocities are d/dt of interpolated alt/range (rel_vel = |v| ground-relative).
One horizontal assumption: LM-3B&#x27;s published ground range is laid along this mission&#x27;s constant-azimuth rhumb (LM-3B itself doglegs).
Az 109 deg from debris-zone notice ZJ385/26 + NOTAMs RKRR D3252/26, RJJJ P5065/26 (zone near 30.28N 126.00E). Flown: LL2 Success 19:25Z.
Pad (LL2): 40.960482N 100.298059E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=109.00 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-10-23T19:25:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
